# 7. Hierarchical Understanding

A powerful principle in vision is hierarchy.

Humans recognize objects step by step.

Example:

```
Pixels
 |
 v
Lines
 |
 v
Shapes
 |
 v
Parts
 |
 v
Objects
 |
 v
Scene
```

For example:

```
pixels
 |
edges
 |
circles
 |
eyes
 |
face
 |
person
```

Deep neural networks naturally learn this hierarchy.

---

# 8. Geometry: Understanding Space

Vision is not only recognizing objects.

It also understands:

* distance
* position
* movement
* 3D structure

Example:

Two cameras:

```
Camera A        Camera B

    \             /

        Object
```

By comparing views:

```
Different perspectives
        |
        v
Depth estimation
        |
        v
3D reconstruction
```

This is called:

* stereo vision
* structure from motion
* 3D reconstruction

